ation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means the position is fundamentally working. On rising-conviction calls, mild soft signals usually reflect the analyst sizing the position more disciplinedly rather than the thesis breaking. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but keeps the per-call rec in place.\"},{\"analysisId\":583,\"transcriptId\":474,\"callDate\":\"2025-01-29T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Meta (META) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":392,\"symbol\":\"META\",\"shortName\":\"Meta\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":52,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":173,\"transcriptId\":33,\"callDate\":\"2025-01-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Complete Solar (CSLR) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":19,\"symbol\":\"SPWR\",\"shortName\":\"SunPower\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":588,\"transcriptId\":479,\"callDate\":\"2025-01-15T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"JPMorgan (JPM) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":396,\"symbol\":\"JPM\",\"shortName\":\"JPMorgan Chase\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On an established ticker we wait for a second confirming quarter before stepping the recommendation up — one strong quarter on a mature name can be noise. Watch this; if next quarter also comes in improving, the trend layer will upgrade.\"},{\"analysisId\":584,\"transcriptId\":475,\"callDate\":\"2024-12-11T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Adobe (ADBE) Q4 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":393,\"symbol\":\"ADBE\",\"shortName\":\"Adobe\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":11,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":156,\"transcriptId\":68,\"callDa