hesisHealth\":\"Weakening\",\"recommendedSize\":10,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The analyst has already flagged the thesis as Weakening on this call, which is a more decisive signal than anything the trend layer would add. The downstream allocator's graduated exit ratchet (trim → trim more → exit over successive quarters of non-improvement) takes over from here, so the trend layer doesn't issue a separate override — it just confirms the deteriorating direction.\"},{\"analysisId\":185,\"transcriptId\":35,\"callDate\":\"2024-11-07T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"The Trade Desk (TTD) Q3 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":28,\"symbol\":\"TTD\",\"shortName\":\"The Trade Desk\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":115,\"transcriptId\":14,\"callDate\":\"2024-11-07T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amprius (AMPX) Q3 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":6,\"symbol\":\"AMPX\",\"shortName\":\"Amprius\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":35,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst stepped conviction up this quarter (higher recommended size, fresh-money gap not widening, no credibility or mitigation concerns). On a speculative ticker (small-cap, volatile, or pre-revenue), waiting for a second confirming quarter often means missing the inflection — these names move fast. The trend layer steps the recommendation up one notch now (Hold → Add) rather than waiting.\"},{\"analysisId\":136,\"transcriptId\":20,\"callDate\":\"2024-11-06T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Eos Energy (EOSE) Q3 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":12,\"symbol\":\"EOSE\",\"shortName\":\"Eos\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":20,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Trim\",\"trendRationale\":\"The per-call recommendation is Trim — the trend layer never upgrades a per-call Trim (we don't second-guess the analyst's deterioration call upward). Trend layer's view: The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":597,\"transcriptId\":488,\"callDate\":\"2024-10-31T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amazon (AMZN) Q3 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":391,\"symbol\":\"AMZN\",\"shortName\":\"Amazon\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"improving\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"Two quarters in a row of strengthening conviction — the analyst keeps raising recommended size while keeping the fresh-money gap tight, with no credibility or mitigation concerns appearing. That's a clean inflection signal across multiple periods, not a one-off. The trend layer steps the recommendation up one notch (Hold → Add).\"},{\"analysisId\":607,\"transcriptId\":498,\"callDate\":\"2024-10-31T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Mastercard (MA) Q3 2024 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":401,\"symbol\":\"MA\",\"shortName\":\"Mastercard\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":250,\"transcriptId\":141,\"callDate\":\"2024-10-30T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Microsoft (MSFT) Q1 2025 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":82,\"symbol\":\"MSFT\",\"shortName\":\"Microsoft\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":55,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for