ement has historically delivered on this kind of headwind) got weaker). At least one of those is a hard signal (credibility breaking down or mitigation track record eroding), which means the deterioration isn't just noise. The trend layer overrides to a trim regardless of what the per-call rec says.\"},{\"analysisId\":697,\"transcriptId\":588,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-27T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Mastercard (MA) Q1 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":401,\"symbol\":\"MA\",\"shortName\":\"Mastercard\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override the per-call recommendation.\"},{\"analysisId\":687,\"transcriptId\":578,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-27T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Amazon (AMZN) Q1 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":391,\"symbol\":\"AMZN\",\"shortName\":\"Amazon\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":47,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"For three quarters running, the analyst has tightened conviction or pulled back on fresh-money allocation (soft signals: the analyst lowered recommended size by 3+ percentage points; and the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)). Normally a streak this long would call for a trim, but the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening and none of the harder warning signs (credibility break, mitigation track record erosion) have fired. On a Strengthening thesis, a soft-only streak usually reflects the analyst getting more disciplined on a winning name — sizing it more carefully — rather than the thesis itself deteriorating. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but doesn't override the per-call recommendation.\"},{\"analysisId\":395,\"transcriptId\":286,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-27T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"First Solar (FSLR) Q1 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":88,\"symbol\":\"FSLR\",\"shortName\":\"First Solar\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Hold\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":null,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"flattening\",\"finalAction\":\"Hold\",\"trendRationale\":\"The thesis just stepped down from Strengthening to Intact, with none of the soft warning signs firing — typical of a growth name maturing into a steady-state cash generator. It's not deteriorating, but the upside is no longer compounding the way it was. The trend layer doesn't automatically act on this: the right call depends on whether there's a higher-conviction candidate to rotate into, which is a Layer 3 (opportunity scanner) decision we haven't built yet. Until then, treat this as a 'on deck for review' signal.\"},{\"analysisId\":283,\"transcriptId\":174,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-26T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Enovix (ENVX) Q1 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":74,\"symbol\":\"ENVX\",\"shortName\":\"Enovix\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":25,\"tier\":\"speculative\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"This quarter showed a single soft signal (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) but the prior quarter was clean. One isolated quarter of softness isn't enough to act on — could just be the analyst tuning position size on a strong call. The trend layer flags it to monitor; if next quarter also comes in soft, the two-soft rule will kick in and we'll consider stepping the recommendation down.\"},{\"analysisId\":690,\"transcriptId\":581,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-25T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Visa (V) Q2 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":394,\"symbol\":\"V\",\"shortName\":\"Visa\",\"tickerStatus\":\"watchlist\",\"perCallRec\":\"Add\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Strengthening\",\"recommendedSize\":45,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"softening\",\"finalAction\":\"Add\",\"trendRationale\":\"The analyst has shown two quarters of soft signals (the gap between recommended size and fresh-money allocation widened by 2+ points (analyst getting more cautious about new buying)) — typically this would prompt the trend layer to step the recommendation down one notch. But the underlying thesis is still rated Strengthening, which means the position is fundamentally working. On rising-conviction calls, mild soft signals usually reflect the analyst sizing the position more disciplinedly rather than the thesis breaking. The trend layer flags this as a watch item but keeps the per-call rec in place.\"},{\"analysisId\":330,\"transcriptId\":221,\"callDate\":\"2023-04-19T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"Tesla (TSLA) Q1 2023 Earnings Call Transcript\",\"tickerId\":35,\"symbol\":\"TSLA\",\"shortName\":\"Tesla\",\"tickerStatus\":\"portfolio\",\"perCallRec\":\"Trim\",\"thesisHealth\":\"Intact\",\"recommendedSize\":35,\"tier\":\"established\",\"trajectory\":\"deteriorating\"